+Rollback or compensation is a new corrective transition. It MUST follow
+Execution → Observation → Verification → Commit against the exact current
+parent. Only a corrective transition that passes verification and is committed
+by the World Kernel within the atomic World-version/receipt/delivery-intent
+unit may create a corrective `WORLD_COMMIT_RECEIPT` and post-commit successful
+outcome event. A failed, rejected, conflicted, or indeterminate correction
+MUST create truthful durable failure or `RECOVERY_REQUIRED` evidence and MUST
+NOT claim successful completion or emit a successful outcome event.
+
